    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0405" n="397" xml:id="pg397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11551: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander of the United States Yangtze Patrol</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Marquart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d485-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-09T20:30:00+08:00">December 9, 1937—8:30
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 9—7:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0009. Nanking city gates closed, many fires burning both sides of river,
                    waterfront area outside city walls practically deserted, intensive bombing by
                    Japanese through day. <hi rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> moved 2 miles up river
                    from present anchorage to facilitate evacuation remaining nationals. U. S. S.
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Guam</hi> standing by Wuhu where 16 United States
                    nationals remain.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
